ikivoyageTitle":"Culiacán"},{"id":"culiacan_wv_difocur","areaId":"culiacan","name":"DIFOCUR","category":"museum","tags":["museums"],"location":{"lat":24.81148,"lng":-107.39355},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"culiacan_wv_difocur","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["difocurculiacan","culiacan"],"hours":{"week":[null,{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Closed Mon; Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"The cultural center of Culiacán. The complex includes various exhibits and small museums. Events take place often at DIFOCUR.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Culiacán"},{"id":"culiacan_wv_ayuntamiento_de_culiacan","areaId":"culiacan","name":"Ayuntamiento de Culiacán","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":24.80706,"lng":-107.39382},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"culiacan_wv_ayuntamiento_de_culiacan","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["ayuntamientodeculiacan","culiacan"],"summary":"Many beautiful murals featuring street scenes in Culiacán and motifs glorifying the sinaloense spirit.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Culiacán"},{"id":"culiacan_wv_tres_rios_water_park","areaId":"culiacan","name":"Tres Ríos Water Park","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":24.80823,"lng":-107.40792},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"culiacan_wv_tres_rios_water_park","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["tresrioswaterpark","culiacan"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"A recreational park at the confluence of the Humaya and Tamazula rivers, where the Culiacán River is born. Not much to see; you get a better view of the confluence from the Dancing Fountains.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Culiacán"},{"id":"culiacan_wv_dancing_fountains","areaId":"culiacan","name":"Dancing Fountains","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":24.81204,"lng":-107.40608},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"culiacan_wv_dancing_fountains","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["dancingfountains","culiacan"],"summary":"A spectacle of hundreds of independent fountains programmed to \"dance\" to the sound of typical Sinaloan music. This show is presented every day in an area of the 3 Ríos Project where the flagpole is located, more specifically, at the confluence of the Humaya and Tamazula rivers. The shows are always given twice at night and always at the same time.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Culiacán"},{"id":"culiacan_wv_el_chapo_s_house","areaId":"culiacan","name":"El Chapo's House","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":24.77598,"lng":-107.41202},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"culiacan_wv_el_chapo_s_house","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["elchaposhouse","culiacan"],"summary":"The surprisingly unassuming residence of famed drug lord Joaquín \"El Chapo\" Guzmán, before he escaped a raid by Mexican marines via a tunnel below the bathtub in 2014. You can't go inside and you might annoy the neighbors.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Culiacán"},{"id":"culiacan_wv_restaurant_huy_fong","areaId":"culiacan","name":"Restaurant Huy Fong 匯豐餐館","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":24.81174,"lng":-107.38411},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"culiacan_wv_restaurant_huy_fong","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["restauranthuyfong","culiacan"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"08:30","close":"20:00"},{"open":"08:30","close":"20:00"},{"open":